{
  "scope": "Contribution-path altitude statistics of the same weighted mixed kernel that produced each aperture's committed prediction (kernel identity = plan design point 1). P10/P50/P90 and band fractions describe the atmospheric branch only; the vacuum branch (tangent above table top, transmission one) is recorded separately and enters the zeroth-moment identity only. Single authoritative implementation of four-aperture height statistics; round2 altitude_quantiles is a historical product generator and its committed June values are the anchor.",
  "kernel_identity": {
    "zeroth_moment_definition": "sum(weights) + vacuum branch == committed prediction",
    "relative_tolerance": 1e-12,
    "tolerance_semantics": "structural reuse makes equality hold by construction; the budget covers float summation-order differences only. Gate failure routing: aperture/kernel-identity errors fix the kernel; pure reproduction differences fix the tolerance definition with written justification, never silently.",
    "band_edges_m": [
      2000.0,
      12000.0
    ],
    "band_semantics": "below 2 km: no aerosol component in the model; 2-12 km: OPAC free troposphere; over 12 km: no component (molecular above; vacuum above the 120 km table top reported separately)"
  },
